 Remote Server Deployment Guide

  Here are the main approaches for deploying your dockerized OTK Assistant to a remote server:
  ---

  🎯 **Option 1: Direct Docker Compose Deployment (Simplest)**


  Prerequisites:

  • A remote Linux server (Ubuntu/Debian/CentOS)
  • SSH access with sudo privileges
  • Domain name (optional, for SSL)


  Steps:

  1. Prepare Remote Server

     1 │# SSH into your server
     2 │ssh user@your-server-ip
     3 │
     4 │# Install Docker & Docker Compose
     5 │curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh
     6 │sudo sh get-docker.sh
     7 │sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
     8 │
     9 │# Install Docker Compose
    10 │sudo curl -L "https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/latest/download/docker-compose-$(uname -s)-$(uname -m)" -o /usr/local/bin/docker-compose
    11 │sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/docker-compose
    12 │
    13 │# Logout and login to apply docker group
    14 │exit
    15 │ssh user@your-server-ip

  2. Transfer Your Application
  Option A: Using Git (Recommended)

     1 │# On remote server
     2 │git clone <your-github-repo-url>
     3 │cd otk-assistant
     4 │git checkout dbloader  # or your branch

  Option B: Using rsync

     1 │# From your local machine
     2 │rsync -avz --exclude 'build' --exclude '.gradle' \
     3 │  /home/oleg/IdeaProjects/otk-assistant/ \
     4 │  user@your-server-ip:/opt/otk-assistant/

  Option C: Using SCP

     1 │# From your local machine, create a tarball first
     2 │cd /home/oleg/IdeaProjects/otk-assistant
     3 │tar -czf otk-app.tar.gz --exclude='build' --exclude='.gradle' .
     4 │
     5 │# Transfer to server
     6 │scp otk-app.tar.gz user@your-server-ip:/opt/
     7 │
     8 │# On server, extract
     9 │ssh user@your-server-ip
    10 │cd /opt
    11 │tar -xzf otk-app.tar.gz -C /opt/otk-assistant

  3. Configure for Production

     1 │# On remote server
     2 │cd /opt/otk-assistant  # or wherever you deployed
     3 │
     4 │# Create production environment file
     5 │cp .env.prod.example .env.prod
     6 │
     7 │# Edit with your settings
     8 │nano .env.prod
     9 │# Set:
    10 │# - Strong POSTGRES_PASSWORD
    11 │# - Your domain names in ALLOWED_ORIGINS
    12 │# - API_BASE_URL with your domain

  4. Set Up SSL (for HTTPS)
  Option A: Let's Encrypt (Free, Recommended)

     1 │# Install Certbot
     2 │sudo apt update
     3 │sudo apt install -y certbot
     4 │
     5 │# Stop nginx temporarily (if running)
     6 │docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml stop nginx
     7 │
     8 │# Get certificate
     9 │sudo certbot certonly --standalone \
    10 │  -d yourdomain.com -d www.yourdomain.com
    11 │
    12 │# Copy certificates
    13 │sudo cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/fullchain.pem nginx/ssl/cert.pem
    14 │sudo cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/privkey.pem nginx/ssl/key.pem
    15 │sudo chmod 644 nginx/ssl/cert.pem
    16 │sudo chmod 600 nginx/ssl/key.pem

  Option B: Use Self-Signed (Testing Only)

     1 │cd scripts
     2 │./generate-ssl-certs.sh

  5. Deploy Application

     1 │# Build and start
     2 │docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml build
     3 │docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
     4 │
     5 │# Check status
     6 │docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml ps
     7 │
     8 │# View logs
     9 │docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml logs -f

  6. Configure Firewall

     1 │# Using UFW (Ubuntu/Debian)
     2 │sudo ufw allow 22/tcp    # SSH
     3 │sudo ufw allow 80/tcp    # HTTP
     4 │sudo ufw allow 443/tcp   # HTTPS
     5 │sudo ufw enable
     6 │
     7 │# Or using firewalld (CentOS/RHEL)
     8 │sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=http
     9 │sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=https
    10 │sudo firewall-cmd --reload

  7. Set Up Auto-Start on Reboot

     1 │# Create systemd service
     2 │sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/otk-assistant.service
     3 │
     4 │# Paste this content:
     5 │[Unit]
     6 │Description=OTK Assistant Docker Compose
     7 │Requires=docker.service
     8 │After=docker.service
     9 │
    10 │[Service]
    11 │Type=oneshot
    12 │RemainAfterExit=yes
    13 │WorkingDirectory=/opt/otk-assistant
    14 │ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/docker-compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
    15 │ExecStop=/usr/local/bin/docker-compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml down
    16 │TimeoutStartSec=0
    17 │
    18 │[Install]
    19 │WantedBy=multi-user.target
    20 │
    21 │# Enable and start
    22 │sudo systemctl enable otk-assistant
    23 │sudo systemctl start otk-assistant

