  🎯 **Option 2: Cloud Provider Deployment**


  **A. AWS (Elastic Beanstalk or EC2)**

  Using EC2:
  1. Launch Ubuntu EC2 instance (t2.medium or larger)
  2. Configure Security Groups (ports 22, 80, 443)
  3. Assign Elastic IP (static IP)
  4. Follow "Option 1" steps above

  Using Elastic Container Service (ECS):
  • Push images to ECR (Amazon's Docker registry)
  • Create ECS task definitions
  • Deploy using Fargate or EC2 launch type
  • More complex but auto-scaling


  **B. DigitalOcean Droplet**


     1 │# Create Droplet (Ubuntu 22.04, 2GB RAM minimum)
     2 │# SSH in and follow Option 1 steps
     3 │# DigitalOcean provides easier networking/firewall UI


  **C. Linode / Vultr / Hetzner**

  Similar to DigitalOcean - create VPS, follow Option 1

  **D. Azure Container Instances**

  • Push images to Azure Container Registry
  • Deploy via Azure Portal or CLI
  • Good for small deployments

